    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d877">

                <pb facs="0934" n="836" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg836"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/974</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 19.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 772</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>A Bill was introduced in congress and referred to a specially elected commission
                    for examination providing for the trial of Tinoco and his adherents for military
                    rebellion and declaring his acts during the time from January 27, 1917 to
                    September 3, 1919, as null and void, with exceptions for the exclusive benefit
                    of the Treasury. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Benjamin F. Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
